  "id": "DrugBank_DB01085 - MONDO_6875",
  "verbalization": "Pilocarpine is implicated in the pathogenesis of Ocular Hypertension through its association with Open-angle Glaucoma, a condition that is itself linked to Ocular Hypertension. The evidence suggests that Pilocarpine may exert a role in the development of Ocular Hypertension via its effects on the eye, as it is indicated in the treatment of Open-angle Glaucoma, which is a known risk factor for Ocular Hypertension. This relationship is supported by the shared indication of Open-angle Glaucoma across multiple drug–disease links, indicating a potential mechanistic overlap. The presence of similar indications for Pilocarpine in different drugs that target similar pathophysiological processes suggests a possible shared mechanism of action, although the exact nature of this mechanism remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of targeting the underlying pathophysiology of Open-angle Glaucoma, which may offer a novel therapeutic approach for Ocular Hypertension.",
